(95% range +0.04 to +0.75). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months; 5 months fell. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Pullman has gotten drier","p_rain":"Pullman's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.36 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.68 to \u22120.04), about \u22124.6 inches since 1898. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 17.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1958 (29.85 in); the driest, 2005 (6.66 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}